.TH CREATE_CHTTPCLIENT_MP 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
create_chttpclient_mp \- create an HTTP client with a custom allocator
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <chttpclient.h>

chttpcli create_chttpclient_mp(ccol_memmgmt_procs_t *mprocs,
                               char **err_str);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Allocates and initialises a new HTTP client.  The connection pool is
NOT created at this point; it is lazily initialised on the first
request.

Default configuration after creation:
  pool_size          = CPU count (resolved on first request)
  connect_timeout_ms = 0 (no timeout)
  request_timeout_ms = 0 (no timeout)
  TLS                = peer and host verification enabled, system CA
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
mprocs    Custom allocator, or NULL for malloc/free.
err_str   Optional; receives a static error string on failure.
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
New client handle, or NULL on failure.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR create_chttpclient (3),
.BR chttpclient_destroy (3),
.BR chttpclient_set_pool_size (3)
